Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:05.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}AI code assistants like Copilot suggest completions, but they make mistakes,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.28,0:00:09.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and programmers have to catch those mistakes before they turn into bugs.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.81,0:00:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}One popular idea is to highlight the tokens the model was least confident about,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.84,0:00:16.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so a person knows where to look.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.86,0:00:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper asks a sharp question: are those generation probabilities actually the right thing to highlight?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.59,0:00:26.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Through a preregistered study with thirty programmers,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.99,0:00:32.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors compare highlighting low-probability tokens against a new edit model that
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.33,0:00:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}instead predicts which tokens a person is likely to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.04,0:00:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The edit model wins on speed, precision of edits, and user preference,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.45,0:00:44.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}showing that generation probabilities alone are not enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.46,0:00:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}AI code assistants are now everywhere, but they are imperfect,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.75,0:00:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a wrong suggestion can quietly plant a bug or a security hole.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.04,0:00:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To catch those mistakes, a programmer first has to notice them, and that is hard,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.33,0:01:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}because people tend to over-trust automation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.62,0:01:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The tricky part is that a single code suggestion is not one decision but hundreds of tiny ones,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.91,0:01:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}one per token.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.20,0:01:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Earlier research on communicating AI uncertainty was built for single-shot decisions like a diagnosis,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.49,0:01:18.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it does not obviously carry over to this token-by-token world.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.08,0:01:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}One natural idea is to highlight uncertain tokens,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.28,0:01:25.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}much like a spell-checker underlines suspect words,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.55,0:01:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the programmer's eye is drawn to the spots that most need review.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.90,0:01:35.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The obvious signal to use is the model's own generation probability: tokens the model
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.34,0:01:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}was least sure about get highlighted.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.71,0:01:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This is an existing strategy, and it even ships in OpenAI's Playground.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.26,0:01:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But nobody had really tested whether low probability actually lines up with where humans need to make edits,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.17,0:01:52.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and that gap is exactly what this paper set out to probe.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.12,0:01:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors ran a preregistered, mixed-methods study with thirty programmers,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.96,0:02:03.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}comparing three ways of presenting the same AI code completions: no highlights at all,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.38,0:02:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}highlights based on generation probability, and highlights based on a new edit model.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.72,0:02:13.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The edit model is the key idea: instead of asking how confident the model was,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.63,0:02:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it predicts which tokens a human is actually likely to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.53,0:02:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This reframes the whole problem,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.54,0:02:23.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from surfacing model uncertainty to surfacing human intervention,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.63,0:02:30.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the authors argue the same recipe could scale up by learning from edit telemetry that products already collect.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.17,0:02:35.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Under the hood, all three tools used the very same Codex model,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.15,0:02:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so any difference in behavior comes purely from how the completion was displayed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.12,0:02:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The generation-probability tool highlighted tokens the model was least confident in,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.10,0:02:47.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}at a seventy-one percent threshold.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.08,0:02:50.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The edit-model tool highlighted tokens most likely to be edited,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.05,0:02:54.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}at a sixty-six percent threshold,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.03,0:02:58.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}using a model trained on nine coders who had previously edited Codex output until their tasks passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.01,0:03:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Crucially,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.99,0:03:06.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the thresholds were chosen so that every condition showed the same total number of highlights,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.96,0:03:10.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the comparison is about which tokens get highlighted, not how many.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.24,0:03:13.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Thirty participants took part,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.17,0:03:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}all experienced Python programmers at a large US technology company,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.53,0:03:21.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}each paid fifty dollars for roughly an hour of their time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.26,0:03:25.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Every person solved three coding problems drawn from LeetCode's easy tier,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.01,0:03:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with a ten-minute cap per task,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.00,0:03:33.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and could run their code and a set of provided unit tests to debug along the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.20,0:03:38.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Task order and which tool went with which task were randomized to keep the comparison fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.04,0:03:43.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The edit model itself was trained earlier, on a separate group of nine coders.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.35,0:03:46.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline result is about speed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.48,0:03:49.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}People finished fastest when using edit-model highlights,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.96,0:03:52.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}at about eight point six minutes on average,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.64,0:03:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and slowest with generation-probability highlights, at about nine point six minutes,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.76,0:04:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with the no-highlight condition sitting in between.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.87,0:04:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The gap between the two highlighting strategies is highly significant,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.14,0:04:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with a p-value of zero point zero zero three.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.89,0:04:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}What makes this striking is that generation-probability highlighting was actually the worst of the three,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.29,0:04:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}slower even than showing no highlights at all,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.09,0:04:20.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so highlighting the wrong tokens can hurt rather than help.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.99,0:04:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To understand why, the authors tracked which tokens survived,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.56,0:04:28.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}meaning they were left unchanged by the participant.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.12,0:04:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Under the edit model, tokens it left un-highlighted survived far more often,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.69,0:04:35.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}about eighty-seven percent of the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.26,0:04:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while tokens it did highlight survived only about thirty-five percent of the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.83,0:04:42.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Compare that to generation-probability highlighting,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.39,0:04:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}where highlighted tokens still survived seventy-four percent of the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.96,0:04:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.53,0:04:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the edit model's highlights closely predict what people actually change,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.10,0:04:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while generation-probability highlights barely move the needle,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.66,0:05:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and all of these differences are extremely significant.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.53,0:05:06.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To put numbers on it: task time dropped from nine point six one minutes with generation-probability
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.80,0:05:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}highlighting to eight point five nine minutes with the edit model,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.98,0:05:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a significant difference at p equals zero point zero zero three.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.03,0:05:20.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Highlighted-token survival fell from seventy-four percent to thirty-five percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.16,0:05:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}showing far tighter alignment with real edits,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.07,0:05:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}at p below zero point zero zero zero one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.67,0:05:27.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And on a seven-point preference scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.07,0:05:34.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}users rated the edit highlights three point nine four versus two point eight eight for generation probability,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.04,0:05:38.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}significant at p equals zero point zero zero one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.44,0:05:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The lesson is simple but pointed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.70,0:05:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}What you highlight matters more than whether you highlight,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.96,0:05:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the right thing to highlight is where people are likely to edit,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.22,0:05:51.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}not where the model happened to be unsure.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.48,0:05:54.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Generation probabilities alone are not enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.75,0:05:57.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Encouragingly,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.01,0:06:01.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}tools like Copilot already log the edits people make to AI suggestions,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.27,0:06:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so that same signal could train an open-world edit model and carry these speed,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.53,0:06:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}precision, and preference gains into everyday coding.
